],"html_id":"t-49565-row12-col0","key":"ixkAXDyt51"},{"type":"tableCell","identifier":"t_49565_row12_col1","label":"T_49565_row12_col1","class":"data row12 col1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"-191","key":"ZtdNsFNLY0"}],"html_id":"t-49565-row12-col1","key":"qvmYnwxqdl"},{"type":"tableCell","identifier":"t_49565_row12_col2","label":"T_49565_row12_col2","class":"data row12 col2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latvia","key":"XV8z49DvBo"}],"html_id":"t-49565-row12-col2","key":"MCHeobxjF4"},{"type":"tableCell","identifier":"t_49565_row12_col3","label":"T_49565_row12_col3","class":"data row12 col3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2021","key":"z2MqkC5UE0"}],"html_id":"t-49565-row12-col3","key":"BJMKGgWoYr"}],"key":"Eq0vuMtAA8"}],"enumerator":"1","html_id":"t-49565","key":"ib9xN63JvC"}],"key":"OCFi1U52Ld"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, in Ireland in 2021, the gap in childhood mortality rates was only 0.59 per 100,000, substantially smaller than the OECD average, about 22 per 100,000.\nThis small difference seems to be due to an unusually low rate for boys, rather than a high rate for girls.\nThis example suggests that the gap in child mortality can be close to zero.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"uBBlsJw1c3"}],"key":"oSjxBLyYsK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rate gap for several causes is negative, which means that in some places and times, the usual pattern is reversed and death rates are higher for women.\nFor these causes, we assume that if the gaps can be negative or positive, they can also be zero.","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"VqsRCmGjFL"}],"key":"iT6gQQkL2c"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some gaps might be harder to close than others.\nThe smallest rate gap for suicide is about 4 per 100,000, reported in Greece in 2002.\nThe OECD average is about 14.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"fdZmbPj48L"}],"key":"mUZS0wmlrc"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To be conservative, we’ll assume that the smallest observed gap is the smallest attainable gap.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"dg3dqbAgih"}],"key":"oODYY4DELq"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The United States","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"GwV6zd1Ho7"}],"identifier":"the-united-states","label":"The United States","html_id":"the-united-states","implicit":true,"key":"F7XJz2Taul"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In 2023, the life expectancy gap in the United States was 5.0 years, close to the OECD average.\nThe following table shows how much this gap would change, according to the model, if we reduced each cause-specific gap to its best attainable level.","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"HPOQ0i13Sw"}],"key":"aZLvcNex0g"},{"type":"include","file":"tables/counterfactuals_usa_2023_le_blog.html","literal":false,"lang":"html","children":[{"type":"table","identifier":"t_c3776","label":"T_c3776","children":[{"type":"tableRow","children":[{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"identifier":"t_c3776_level0_col0","label":"T_c3776_level0_col0","class":"col_heading level0 col0","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cause","key":"fUu5vJTX4o"}],"html_id":"t-c3776-level0-col0","key":"oJNhB0TPRx"},{"t