en":[{"type":"text","value":"The following figure shows the results graphically, with 94% credible intervals.","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"NEAH8g2kL9"}],"key":"ksfzmfzNf6"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/LifeExpectancy//build/counterfactual_effec-57653c13dc17b9edb7b29eb3126ca03d.png","alt":"Counterfactual effects: hypothetical change in life expectancy gap for each cause-specific death rate, United States (2023), 94% credible intervals.","width":"80%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"LLBv5fzlqz","urlSource":"figs/counterfactual_effects_usa_2023_le_bayesian.png","urlOptimized":"/LifeExpectancy//build/counterfactual_effec-57653c13dc17b9edb7b29eb3126ca03d.webp"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Counterfactual effects: hypothetical change in life expectancy gap for each cause-specific death rate, United States (2023), 94% credible intervals.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"BPZPKV0ZAD"}],"key":"KEhtZTYPiX"}],"key":"zT8K1LvoeO"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"Y3l4NkU2P5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Road traffic has the largest potential impact — reducing the death rate gap to Iceland’s 2017 level would close the life expectancy gap by 0.81 years.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"lz8rkTCV2g"}],"key":"R4UWT0i9AZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drug disorders are second — reducing the gap to Japan’s 2013 level (essentially zero) would close the life expectancy gap by 0.77 years.","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"K9mqDA9SqD"}],"key":"AvMsrKVILt"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And if the rate gap due to suicide could be reduced from 18 to 4 per 100,000, the model predicts the life expectancy gap would close by 0.52 years.","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"FzpsbnsVyi"}],"key":"syfjGRYfva"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For homicide, liver disease, cancer, and alcohol, the potential impact is smaller but still meaningful.\nThe potential impact of childhood mortality and injury is smaller still, and for COVID-19 in 2023 it is near zero.","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"WNUlAHh7ec"}],"key":"U5e5TuzwDN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For lung disease, the gender gap in the U.S. is negative, meaning that the death rate is higher for women.\nSo if we close this gap to zero, the life expectancy gap might grow by 0.18 years.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"Hl6efW2xNs"}],"key":"k6yX4okf3r"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And for cardiovascular disease and diabetes, the estimated coefficient is negative, which means that if we reduce the rate gap, the model predicts that the life expectancy gap would grow.\nHowever, as we discussed in ","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"XHZXByVpXO"},{"type":"link","url":"https://allendowney.substack.com/p/what-drives-the-life-expectancy-gender","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the previous article","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"FHxnAbdyKM"}],"urlSource":"https://allendowney.substack.com/p/what-drives-the-life-expectancy-gender","key":"LZGWie0Yf1"},{"type":"text","value":", these negative coefficients might be explained by competing risks — if general health outcomes are better, more people live long enough to die from diseases of aging, so those rates tend to be higher.\nIf that’s true, the counterfactual assumption might not hold — that is, if an intervention is able to reduce these gaps, it’s not clear what effect that would have on life expectancy.","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"CqOxjnx6iz"}],"key":"RvmPn7bRpR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"But for the other causes of death, the counterfactual assumption is plausible.\nFor example, if the rate gap due to drug disorders closes — which is likely as overall rates have already started to fall — it is reasonable to expect the life expectancy gap to close, other things being equal.","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"key":"EL84Ry5BxW"}],"key":"MUWKz0um5S"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The total of the gap-closing effects is about 3.1 years, which suggests that together they could reduce the life expectancy gap from 5.0 to 2.9 years.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"EhrYPpAunh"}],"key":"hfksuz2Xdk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In reality these effects are likely to interact.\nFor example, a decrease in consumption of alcohol would directly affect death rates due to alcohol, and indirectly affect rates due to liver disease, cancer, road traffic, accidents, suicide, homicide, and possibly drug disorders.\nWith these kinds of interactions, the total effect of multiple interventions might be larger or smaller than the sum of the estimates from the model.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"A4y1VedhWs"}],"key":"LTWP2SC8mC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nevertheless, the magnitudes of the contributions indicate which interventions have the most potential to reduce the life expectancy gap.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"puXmIwawDk"}],"key":"DfpDeGoTzB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following figure shows how the positive contributions to the gap have changed over time.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"wsNLwmZmgP"}],"key":"PCplLZxAIR"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/LifeExpectancy//build/positive_contributio-53b82496069c2157bb2de54552801a09.png","alt":"Stacked positive contributions to the life expectancy gap, United States (2000–2023).","width":"80%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"F06XkbTLRb","urlSource":"figs/positive_contributions_stacked_area_usa_le.png","urlOptimized":"/LifeExpectancy//build/positive_contributio-53b82496069c2157bb2de54552801a09.webp"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stacked positive contributions to the life expectancy gap, United States (2000–2023).","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"cubkUcwlSH"}],"key":"BZSnHmDSJo"}],"key":"KAEtk10m9J"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"fZpPOjIzKo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The total has generally increased, driven by a large increase in the contribution of drug disorders and smaller increases in the contributions of suicide and road traffic.\nBut this pattern is unusual; in most OECD countries, the total contribution decreased over this period, as we’ll see in the next article.","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"yhIJIqmXzZ"}],"key":"mMIsVR5jhO"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":95,"column":1},"end":{"line":95,"column":1}},"key":"M4dR8urH7m"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next: ","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"key":"Zp7WEeeSsF"},{"type":"link","url":"/blog4-international","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Blog Post 4: International patterns and policy","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"key":"dlslHCHUy7"}],"urlSource":"blog4_international.md","dataUrl":"/blog4-international.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"sgVBGYPP3L"}],"key":"BFlDZGmN4F"}],"key":"ptkaCLAbpF"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":1},"end":{"line":99,"column":1}},"key":"a4A7fKdbLn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":1},"end":{"line":101,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source: Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation. Used with permission. All rights reserved.","key":"S8Ye4t9bnM"}],"key":"qrrWMlZ37e"}],"key":"qE3Gt2NEk0"}],"key":"E7iw5eqpjv"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"What Drives the Life Expectancy Gender Gap?","short_title":"2. What Drives the Gap?","url":"/blog2-model","group":"Blog Series"},"next":{"title":"International Patterns in the Life Expectancy Gap","short_title":"4. International Patterns","url":"/blog4-international","group":"Blog Series"}}},"domain":"https://allendowney.github.io"}